This page documents the various deployment methods available for SuperTokens with PostgreSQL database support. It covers both Docker container deployment and Kubernetes deployment options, along with configuration approaches for each method. For specific details about container configuration, see Container Configuration and for environment variables reference, see Environment Variables.
SuperTokens PostgreSQL can be deployed using several methods, each with its own advantages depending on your infrastructure requirements.
Sources: README.md3-7 helm-chart/README.md1-56
SuperTokens PostgreSQL can be deployed as a Docker container with various configuration options.
The simplest way to deploy SuperTokens is using the default Docker container:
