SuperTokens can be configured using environment variables or a custom configuration file.
Sources: README.md9-13 README.md14-70 README.md89-103
SuperTokens can be configured using environment variables, with many options available for customizing behavior:
| Category | Key Environment Variables | 
|---|---|
| Core | API_KEYS,SUPERTOKENS_HOST,SUPERTOKENS_PORT,ACCESS_TOKEN_VALIDITY, etc. | 
| Database | POSTGRESQL_CONNECTION_URI,POSTGRESQL_USER,POSTGRESQL_PASSWORD,POSTGRESQL_HOST, etc. | 
| Token Settings | ACCESS_TOKEN_VALIDITY,REFRESH_TOKEN_VALIDITY,EMAIL_VERIFICATION_TOKEN_LIFETIME, etc. | 
| Security | API_KEYS,IP_ALLOW_REGEX,IP_DENY_REGEX,PASSWORD_HASHING_ALG, etc. | 
| Server Config | MAX_SERVER_POOL_SIZE,BASE_PATH,DISABLE_TELEMETRY, etc. | 
For a complete list of environment variables, see Environment Variables.
Sources: README.md14-70
Instead of environment variables, you can use a custom config.yaml file:
Key requirements for the configuration file:
core_config_version: 0host: "0.0.0.0"postgresql_config_version: 0info_log_path: null (to log in docker logs)error_log_path: null (to log in docker logs)Sources: README.md89-103
For Kubernetes environments, SuperTokens provides a Helm chart for easy deployment.
Sources: helm-chart/README.md1-56
To deploy SuperTokens on Kubernetes using Helm:
Sources: helm-chart/README.md1-56
The Helm chart provides many configuration options through the values.yaml file:
| Category | Key Configuration Values | 
|---|---|
| Database | database.uri,database.host,database.port,database.user,database.password,database.name | 
| Token Settings | accessTokenValidity,refreshTokenValidity,accessTokenBlacklisting,accessTokenSigningKeyDynamic | 
| Core Settings | maxServerPoolSize,disableTelemetry,basePath | 
| Service Configuration | service.type,service.port,service.targetPort,service.nodePort | 
| Autoscaling | autoscaling.enabled,autoscaling.minReplicas,autoscaling.maxReplicas,autoscaling.targetCPUUtilizationPercentage | 
| Security | apiKeys.enabled,apiKeys.keys,existingSecret | 
Sources: helm-chart/README.md7-56
To enable autoscaling for SuperTokens in Kubernetes:
This configures the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler to automatically scale SuperTokens pods based on CPU utilization.
Sources: helm-chart/README.md17-20
For enhanced security, you can use existing Kubernetes secrets instead of embedding sensitive values in Helm values:
When existingSecret is specified, any database and apiKeys options are ignored in favor of the values in the secret.
Sources: helm-chart/README.md30-31
Regardless of the deployment method, SuperTokens needs to be configured to connect to a PostgreSQL database or use an in-memory database.
Sources: README.md122-126
SuperTokens can connect to PostgreSQL using:
Connection URI:
POSTGRESQL_CONNECTION_URI="postgresql://username:password@host:port/dbName"
Individual parameters:
POSTGRESQL_USER="postgresqlUser"
POSTGRESQL_HOST="postgres-host"
POSTGRESQL_PORT="5432"  
POSTGRESQL_PASSWORD="password"
POSTGRESQL_DATABASE_NAME="supertokens"  # Optional, defaults to "supertokens"
In-memory database (default if no PostgreSQL configuration provided):
Sources: README.md122-126 README.md57-70
Sources: README.md122-126
| Deployment Method | Ideal For | Key Benefits | Configuration Approach | 
|---|---|---|---|
| Standard Docker | Simple environments, development | Easy setup, minimal requirements | Environment variables or config.yaml | 
| Docker with Read-Only FS | Production, enhanced security | Improved security posture | Requires volume mount for temp files | 
| Docker with TCP Keepalive | Production, network stability | Better network reliability | Configure keepalive sysctl parameters | 
| Kubernetes Basic | Container orchestration environments | Integration with K8s ecosystem | Helm values.yaml | 
| Kubernetes with Autoscaling | Dynamic workloads | Automatic scaling based on load | Enable autoscaling in Helm values | 
| Kubernetes with Existing Secrets | Production, security-focused | Separate secret management | Reference existing K8s secrets | 
Sources: README.md1-157 helm-chart/README.md1-56
